# AI Hub UI — environment variables
#
# Values below reflect the real AICOE-Terraform-provisioned dev environment
# (project gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui, region europe-west3), confirmed against:
#   - AICOE-Terraform/terraform/2-foundations/gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui.tf
#   - AICOE-Terraform/terraform/6-workloads/6a-gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui/main.tf
#   - AICOE-Terraform/terraform/5-network-psc/main.tf
#   - AICOE-Terraform/terraform/envs/dev/terraform.tfvars
# See docs/deployment.md for the full breakdown and source citations.
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development overrides. Next.js loads
# .env.local automatically; server-side vars come from server/config/env.ts
# defaults or process.env, client-side VITE_* vars come from shared/config.ts.
#
# GitLab CI: set the same VITE_* keys as environment-scoped variables (sandbox / dev / prod)
# and pass them as Docker --build-arg in build-and-push (see .gitlab-ci.yml and docs/deployment.md).
#
# NOTE — two Cloud Run URLs below are marked <LOOK-UP-REQUIRED>. They cannot be
# hardcoded because Cloud Run URLs are assigned at deploy time; resolve them with:
#   gcloud run services describe translation-api-service --project=gclt-aicoe-dev-st --region=europe-west3 --format='value(status.url)'
#   gcloud run services describe sales-research-application --project=gclt-aicoe-dev-st --region=europe-west3 --format='value(status.url)'

# ── Translation API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Internal Apigee origin, reached over the PSC endpoint (10.110.73.10) —
# private DNS record aihub-api.aicoedev-int.colt.net (terraform/5-network-psc/main.tf).
# Diagnostics/display only — the browser calls the BFF's own /api/translation/v1 route,
# never this origin directly.
VITE_TRANSLATION_API_ORIGIN=https://aihub-api.aicoedev-int.colt.net
# Cloud Run .run.app URL of translation-api-service (project gclt-aicoe-dev-st,
# region europe-west3) — IAM identity token audience, not the DNS host above.
VITE_TRANSLATION_CLOUD_RUN_URL=<LOOK-UP-REQUIRED: gcloud run services describe translation-api-service --project=gclt-aicoe-dev-st --region=europe-west3 --format='value(status.url)'>

# ── Sales Agent API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SALES_API_ORIGIN=https://aihub-api.aicoedev-int.colt.net
VITE_SALES_CLOUD_RUN_URL=<LOOK-UP-REQUIRED: gcloud run services describe sales-research-application --project=gclt-aicoe-dev-st --region=europe-west3 --format='value(status.url)'>

# ── Contract management API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not yet provisioned in AICOE-Terraform — confirm with the owning team before
# setting a real value for non-local environments.
VITE_CONTRACTS_API_BASE=http://localhost:5010/api

# ── GCP metadata (display / diagnostics) ─────────────────────────────────────
VITE_GCP_PROJECT_ID=gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui
VITE_GCP_PROJECT_NUMBER=<LOOK-UP-REQUIRED: gcloud projects describe gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui --format='value(projectNumber)'>
VITE_GCP_REGION=europe-west3

# ── TLS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by local dev tooling only; not meaningful inside Cloud Run, which
# reaches Apigee over a private PSC endpoint.
VITE_TLS_CA_FILE=certs/colt-internal-ca.pem

# ── Server-side runtime variables (server/config/env.ts) ─────────────────────
# These are NOT VITE_/build-time — they're read directly via process.env at
# runtime by the Next.js server. Set them as Cloud Run --set-env-vars in CI,
# or in .env.local (not committed) for local development.
#
# ENTRA_TENANT_ID=<Entra ID tenant ID>
# ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=<AI-BFF app registration client ID>
# ENTRA_REDIRECT_URI=https://aihub.aicoedev-int.colt.net/auth/callback
# ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET_SECRET_NAME=entra-bff-client-secret
# GCP_PROJECT_ID=gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui
# GCP_PROJECT_NUMBER=<project number, see VITE_GCP_PROJECT_NUMBER above>
# GCP_KMS_KEY_RING=aihub-ew3
# GCP_KMS_KEY_NAME=session
# GCP_KMS_LOCATION=europe-west3
# APIGEE_CLIENT_KEY_SECRET_NAME=apigee-bff-client-key
# TRANSLATION_API_ORIGIN=https://aihub-api.aicoedev-int.colt.net
# SALES_API_ORIGIN=https://aihub-api.aicoedev-int.colt.net

# ── Per-environment reference ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# sandbox — currently maps to the same gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui project as dev;
#           there is no separate sandbox GCP project in AICOE-Terraform today.
#           Confirm with the platform team before assuming otherwise.
# dev     — set GitLab environment-scoped vars on branch `dev`
# prod    — NOT YET PROVISIONED. AICOE-Terraform's envs/prod/terraform.tfvars
#           still has REPLACE_ME placeholders for every prod project ID.
#
# GitLab CI/CD variables (group + per-environment scope) — see docs/deployment.md
# for the full list and Terraform-confirmed values:
#   WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_PROJECT_NUMBER, WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_POOL (gitlab-pool),
#   WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_PROVIDER (gitlab-provider), SERVICE_ACCOUNT
#   (tf-deployer@gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui.iam.gserviceaccount.com),
#   GCP_PROJECT_ID (gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui), GCP_REGION (europe-west3),
#   ARTIFACT_REPO (containers), IMAGE_NAME (aihub-bff),
#   CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE (aihub-bff), CLOUD_RUN_NETWORK (gclt-aicoe-dev-vpc),
#   CLOUD_RUN_SUBNET (gclt-aicoe-dev-cloudrun-ew3),
#   CLOUD_RUN_SA (aihub-bff-sa@gclt-aicoe-dev-aihub-ui.iam.gserviceaccount.com)
#
# IMPORTANT: this repo's GitLab project path is not yet in the shared WIF
# provider's allowed_repositories allow-list (AICOE-Terraform/terraform/envs/dev/terraform.tfvars).
# WIF-authenticated CI jobs (build-and-push, deploy-cloud-run) will fail until
# the platform team adds it and re-applies 0-bootstrap. See docs/deployment.md §3.2.
